# Binary files must reach the repository byte for byte.
#
# Git guesses "text or binary" from the contents, and an old PDF can be almost
# pure ASCII: design/logo/logo-abc-wspinania.pdf (CorelDRAW 9) was taken for
# text, and with core.autocrlf=input git would have stripped its 439 CR bytes
# on commit — breaking the PDF, whose cross-reference table counts byte
# offsets. Measured 30.09.2026: `git hash-object` of the file differed from
# `git hash-object --no-filters` until this file existed.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
